      "content": "Your feelings are completely valid, and it must be incredibly tough to feel this way. It’s important to recognize that your presence alone can bring immense joy and support to your family—it may not always feel that way, but it does. However, finding ways to ease their burden is important too. Maybe small changes or accepting help could bring some relief. It’s worth having an open conversation with your family about how you’re feeling so they can understand and possibly work together towards finding a solution. Remember, it's a team effort, and you’re not alone in feeling this way.",
